From: Clay Warren
Subject: Use the available Clang preprocessor for Windows ARM64 assembly

The Windows ARM64 recipe supplies clang-cpp, while the default cpp executable
is absent. Keep the existing -undef and _WIN32 arguments for target-neutral
preprocessing before translating to armasm64 syntax.

--- a/tools/gas-preprocessor.pl
+++ b/tools/gas-preprocessor.pl
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 }
 if ($as_type eq "armasm") {
 
-    $preprocess_c_cmd[0] = "cpp";
+    $preprocess_c_cmd[0] = "clang-cpp";
     push(@preprocess_c_cmd, "-undef");
     # Normally a preprocessor for windows would predefine _WIN32,
     # but we're using any generic system-agnostic preprocessor "cpp"
